# ---------------------------------------------------------------- source data
# The PNOA LiDAR block and orthophoto mosaic are several GB and are freely
# redistributed by the CNIG. See the README for download instructions.
*.laz
*.tif
*.tiff
*.gpkg
*.zip
PNOA_MA_OF_*.xml

# ---------------------------------------------------------------- private
# Internal design document; kept locally, deliberately not published.
zaragoza_eclipse_visibility_web_plan.md

# ---------------------------------------------------------------- generated
data/output/
data/intermediate/

# The viewer's data products ARE committed - they are what GitHub Pages serves,
# and regenerating them needs the multi-GB LiDAR block that is not in this repo.
# Paths are per-city (viewer/public/data/<city>/) so a second city cannot overwrite
# the first. The orthophoto tile set is never committed: it was 671 MB, so the viewer
# reads the IGN WMTS instead (see package_tiles.py).
viewer/public/data/*/tiles/rgb/

# 3D buildings (pipeline/export_buildings.py). Local experiment only. The viewer hides
# its 3D control when this file is absent, which is the deployed case, so nothing in
# the committed data advertises a feature the live site does not have.
viewer/public/data/*/buildings.geojson

# Linares and Jaén are local experiments and are not deployed. Only Zaragoza is
# published, so their data products stay out of the repository rather than inflating
# a site that does not serve them.
viewer/public/data/linares/
viewer/public/data/jaen/

viewer/dist/
linares_run.sh

# ---------------------------------------------------------------- environments
.venv/
node_modules/
__pycache__/
*.pyc
.pytest_cache/
*.log

# docs/overview.png is committed deliberately (README illustration)
!docs/overview.png
